[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date-swap report into one ticket and called it known:
one parser bug, one fix queued. Reading every merged report's body shows that's two problems,
not one.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471's own cause table already renders this: the <code>hint</code> row shows "not this ticket
— no ticket of its own." This page just spells out what to do about it.
</Callout>

## What #4471 actually holds

<BreakdownTable ticket={4471} />

- **parser** — the shared parser reads every date month first; day-first tenants (by
  `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, see `causes.ts: dayFirst()`) get it flipped. This is #4471's real bug,
  at its real count: 379, including the 5 reports the desk read as a one-day move rather than
  a month/day swap. `causeOf()` assigns cause by tenant + channel only, and `causes.ts`'s own
  comment on `readAs()` says those 5 are "counted where they're filed, footnoted under it" —
  parser reports, read differently, not a different bug. The footnote above says so.
- **hint** — `booking-v3`'s own `MM/DD` hint causes the opposite flip on day-first tenants who
  type what the hint tells them. Same user-visible symptom, different code path. `causes.ts`'s
  own comment calls this "a different bug" from the parser — that's why it's a second ticket,
  not folded into the first.

## Why this matters

A ticket that is "known" because its headline count and its biggest cause agree can still hide
a second cause with no ticket of its own. The numbers above are computed from the same
`reports-4471.json`/`desk-notes.json` this export shipped with — nothing here is typed into
the page. (An earlier pass here also split the one-day-read reports into a third, separate
problem; the kb's own code and comments say that's wrong — they're parser reports, filed and
footnoted, not a new cause.)

## What happened

Filed as [#6 (parser, 379)](https://github.com/titusandronicu/mega-dev/issues/6) and
[#7 (hint, 33)](https://github.com/titusandronicu/mega-dev/issues/7). Engineering closed #4471
on 05 Oct: #6 fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`); #7 won't fix — the `booking-v3`
form was retired. See [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) for the desk's own closed page.

